    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Could be partly, and you can check it directly:\n\n1. Compare section B windows **before vs. after 16:10** (the hotfix). If stalled_after_error is inflated mostly before 16:10, missing events are making windows look idle.\n2. Compare with `possibly_incomplete == False` only. If B still has ~19%, it's probably a real difference (different TA, harder part of the lab, time of day).\n\n```python\ndf[\"after_fix\"] = pd.to_datetime(df.window_start) >= \"2025-11-12 16:10\"\ndf[df.section == \"B\"].groupby(\"after_fix\").label.value_counts(normalize=True).unstack()\n```\n\nMissing edit events would make a window look like \"no edit after error,\" so the bias goes exactly in the stalled direction. Worth ruling out before anyone interprets the section difference."
     ]
    },
